# Floor widgets: footprints lie under the creatures (client/BASE.md 0078; owner debug item 14, z-index of the new effects). Tile:setWidget widgets are drawn by MapView::drawTileWidget in the foreground pass, over walls, items, creatures and even the light, so the cosmetic footprints (game_cosmeticfx) covered everything. New Tile:setFloorWidget(widget) / getFloorWidget() / removeFloorWidget(): the widget is placed like a tile widget (centred, moved by its margins) but drawn in MapView::drawFloor next to the ground effects (after the tile's bottom layer, before its creatures, top items and effects; in the negative-offset pass after every bottom layer). Tile::clean destroys it. The overlay module game_cosmeticfx uses it when the engine has it and falls back to setWidget. C++ only. Applies after 0001-0076 (tile.h/.cpp, mapview.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp).
